The Operating System's IP stack inspects the IP Packet:

IP Destination Verification: The OS checks the Destination IP address:

Verifies the packet is addressed to this host (e.g., 192.168.1.8).

Header Checksum & Options: Verifies the IP header checksum for transmission errors and checks flags (such as reassembling fragmented IP packets if needed).

De-encapsulation: The OS strips off the Layer 3 IP Header.
